0
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,630


1
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:06,790
Today we'll discuss polar coordinate systems.

2
00:00:06,790 --> 00:00:08,790
And we'll start from Cartesian coordinate system

3
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:11,670
and look at the correspondence of a position vector

4
00:00:11,670 --> 00:00:14,130
in polar coordinate system.

5
00:00:14,130 --> 00:00:21,700
So for point p, the position of this point p

6
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:25,180
in a Cartesian coordinate system is

7
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:26,840
uniquely defined by a vector.

8
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:29,350
So we draw our Cartesian coordinate system

9
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:36,790
starting with an origin o and a unit vector, i hat and j hat.

10
00:00:36,790 --> 00:00:41,930
And we uniquely define the position vector

11
00:00:41,930 --> 00:00:44,920
as this vector r that tells us where this particle

12
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:48,470
p is in our coordinate system.

13
00:00:48,470 --> 00:00:55,280
This vector r is then defined as its component

14
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:57,470
in the i hat direction, which we'll call x.

15
00:00:57,470 --> 00:01:00,530
So it will be x in the i hat direction.

16
00:01:00,530 --> 00:01:06,380
And its component in the j hat direction, which we'll call y.

17
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:09,675
So it'll be plus y in the j hat direction.

18
00:01:09,675 --> 00:01:12,290


19
00:01:12,290 --> 00:01:14,870
The magnitude of this position vector

20
00:01:14,870 --> 00:01:17,510
is now just going to be the hypotenuse of this right angle

21
00:01:17,510 --> 00:01:20,750
triangle, which side of magnitude

22
00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:23,900
x here and magnitude y here.

23
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:27,470
So the magnitude of this vector is going to be,

24
00:01:27,470 --> 00:01:30,710
then, the square root of this side square, that's

25
00:01:30,710 --> 00:01:34,840
x square, plus this side square, which is y square.

26
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:37,570


27
00:01:37,570 --> 00:01:40,720
Now in the polar coordinate system,

28
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:44,330
we define a new unit vector, r hat,

29
00:01:44,330 --> 00:01:47,980
which is pointing in the direction of the position

30
00:01:47,980 --> 00:01:50,140
vector r.

31
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:52,450
Then the second unit vector, theta hat

32
00:01:52,450 --> 00:01:57,910
will then be perpendicular to this r hat direction.

33
00:01:57,910 --> 00:02:03,850
So let's rewrite the position of the point here.

34
00:02:03,850 --> 00:02:05,165
And the point will be p.

35
00:02:05,165 --> 00:02:09,919


36
00:02:09,919 --> 00:02:15,230
In this polar coordinate system, now the vector,

37
00:02:15,230 --> 00:02:18,240
the position vector r would have a certain magnitude

38
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:22,014
r in the r hat direction.

39
00:02:22,014 --> 00:02:23,430
But there should be correspondence

40
00:02:23,430 --> 00:02:25,440
between the Cartesian coordinate system

41
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:26,970
and the polar coordinate system.

42
00:02:26,970 --> 00:02:29,280
That is that this magnitude is still the same,

43
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:34,080
regardless of which unit vectors I choose to represent them in.

44
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:37,980
So this magnitude of r is exactly the square root

45
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:39,530
of x squared plus y squared.

46
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:43,650


47
00:02:43,650 --> 00:02:46,170
So for consistency, let's just take the magnitude

48
00:02:46,170 --> 00:02:49,770
of the vector in polar coordinate system.

49
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:53,280
So we say that this has a magnitude which is r,

50
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:54,720
and it's in the r hat direction.

51
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:56,910
So we take the magnitude of r hat direction.

52
00:02:56,910 --> 00:03:00,360
But since r hat is a unit vector, the magnitude of r hat

53
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,440
is just one.

54
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:04,890
So this is just going to be r times one, which is r.

55
00:03:04,890 --> 00:03:10,640
So in fact, if we write down the magnitude of this vector

56
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:14,370
is r in polar coordinate system and it's exactly

57
00:03:14,370 --> 00:03:18,090
square root of x square plus y square

58
00:03:18,090 --> 00:03:20,200
in Cartesian coordinate system.

59
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:24,510
So this is one correspondence between polar coordinate system

60
00:03:24,510 --> 00:03:25,870
and Cartesian coordinate system.

61
00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:30,469


62
00:03:30,469 --> 00:03:32,010
To further look at the correspondence

63
00:03:32,010 --> 00:03:34,830
between Cartesian and polar coordinate system,

64
00:03:34,830 --> 00:03:39,000
let's consider this angle that the position vector r makes

65
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,310
with respect to the x-axis.

66
00:03:42,310 --> 00:03:45,700
And let's define this angle as theta.

67
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:48,710
Then by looking at the same right angle triangle,

68
00:03:48,710 --> 00:03:51,960
we will know that x is the adjacent.

69
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:55,290
Therefore, x can be written as the magnitude

70
00:03:55,290 --> 00:03:59,460
of r times cosine of theta.

71
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:01,710
And y is the opposite.

72
00:04:01,710 --> 00:04:05,280
So y is going to be the magnitude of the position

73
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:09,660
vector r times sine of theta.

74
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:12,750
Since we know that the magnitude can

75
00:04:12,750 --> 00:04:16,709
be written as just a r as a quantity,

76
00:04:16,709 --> 00:04:19,410
so we're just going to simplify this expression

77
00:04:19,410 --> 00:04:23,810
and say it's r cosine theta, and here, r times sine of theta.

78
00:04:23,810 --> 00:04:27,800


79
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:30,590
All these expressions now are self-consistent.

80
00:04:30,590 --> 00:04:34,790
If I take x square plus y square,

81
00:04:34,790 --> 00:04:37,730
I get now r-squared cosine squared

82
00:04:37,730 --> 00:04:43,400
theta plus r square sine squared theta.

83
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:47,990
I can factorize r square and get cosine square theta

84
00:04:47,990 --> 00:04:50,660
plus sine square theta.

85
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:54,510
And this expression is 1.

86
00:04:54,510 --> 00:04:58,020
Therefore, x square plus y square in fact

87
00:04:58,020 --> 00:04:59,750
gives you, again, r square, which

88
00:04:59,750 --> 00:05:01,340
is consistent with the expression

89
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:02,975
that we had just derived there.

90
00:05:02,975 --> 00:05:06,440


91
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:09,550
The next correspondence that we need to derive between polar

92
00:05:09,550 --> 00:05:11,512
and Cartesian coordinate system is

93
00:05:11,512 --> 00:05:12,970
the correspondence between the unit

94
00:05:12,970 --> 00:05:18,010
vectors i hat j hat and r hat theta hat.

95
00:05:18,010 --> 00:05:22,990
For that list, redraw the vectors i hat and j hat.

96
00:05:22,990 --> 00:05:27,960


97
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:31,640
A vector is fully defined by its magnitude and its direction.

98
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:33,800
So I can redraw r hat and theta hat

99
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:38,060
to have the same origin as i hat and j hat.

100
00:05:38,060 --> 00:05:42,230
But notice that r hat is exactly in the direction

101
00:05:42,230 --> 00:05:45,830
of the full position vector r, which is making an angle

102
00:05:45,830 --> 00:05:48,840
theta with the x-axis.

103
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:51,920
Therefore, r hat is making an angle theta

104
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:56,540
with the x-axis, which is the i hat direction.

105
00:05:56,540 --> 00:06:02,800
So I can draw my unit vector r hat

106
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:08,710
as making an angle theta with the i hat direction.

107
00:06:08,710 --> 00:06:11,500
So it's easier to see, then, that the perpendicular

108
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:15,917
component which is theta hat will be pointing this way,

109
00:06:15,917 --> 00:06:17,500
and it will be perpendicular to r hat.

110
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:20,020


111
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:23,850
It's also helpful to know that if this is an angle theta,

112
00:06:23,850 --> 00:06:25,520
this is 90 degrees.

113
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:27,130
Therefore this, by correspondence,

114
00:06:27,130 --> 00:06:32,310
you can solve that this angle is also theta.

115
00:06:32,310 --> 00:06:35,690
So let's decompose now r hat and theta hat

116
00:06:35,690 --> 00:06:38,480
as a function of i hat j hat using this picture.

117
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:41,990


118
00:06:41,990 --> 00:06:44,340
So we can write down r hat.

119
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:46,580
Notice r hat is a unit vector.

120
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:49,815
So if I now look at the projection on the i hat and j

121
00:06:49,815 --> 00:06:56,550
hat, if this is a unit vector, so it has a magnitude 1,

122
00:06:56,550 --> 00:06:58,740
the component on the i hat direction

123
00:06:58,740 --> 00:07:00,940
is just going to be the adjacent, which

124
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:04,385
is cosine of theta.

125
00:07:04,385 --> 00:07:08,660
So cosine of theta times magnitude 1

126
00:07:08,660 --> 00:07:11,450
in the i hat direction.

127
00:07:11,450 --> 00:07:13,400
And then r hat is also going to have

128
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:16,940
a component in the positive j hat direction, which

129
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:19,500
is going to be the opposite.

130
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:24,373
So it's going to be sine of theta in the j hat direction.

131
00:07:24,373 --> 00:07:27,480


132
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:32,530
Now let's look at the theta hat vector.

133
00:07:32,530 --> 00:07:35,680
Notice that theta hat actually projects

134
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:40,100
and has a component opposite of the i hat direction.

135
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:42,440
So i hat is pointing this way.

136
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:45,530
theta hat actually has a component in this direction,

137
00:07:45,530 --> 00:07:48,230
so opposite of i hat direction.

138
00:07:48,230 --> 00:07:50,540
So it's going to have a component in the minus i hat

139
00:07:50,540 --> 00:07:51,504
direction.

140
00:07:51,504 --> 00:07:54,110


141
00:07:54,110 --> 00:07:56,000
And the magnitude of that component

142
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:01,100
is better seen by looking at this right angle triangle,

143
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:04,890
where this is the angle theta.

144
00:08:04,890 --> 00:08:08,810
So the magnitude now is going to be the opposite side, which

145
00:08:08,810 --> 00:08:14,740
is a sine of theta times the magnitude of theta hat.

146
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:16,310
So theta hat is a unit vector.

147
00:08:16,310 --> 00:08:20,170
So it's a 1 times sine of theta, and this component

148
00:08:20,170 --> 00:08:24,200
is in the minus i hat direction.

149
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:27,220
theta hat also has a component in the positive j hat

150
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:30,250
direction.

151
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:32,230
And the magnitude of that component

152
00:08:32,230 --> 00:08:37,429
is going to be this much, which is the adjacent side.

153
00:08:37,429 --> 00:08:40,940
So it's going to be cosine of theta in the j hat direction.

154
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:43,530


155
00:08:43,530 --> 00:08:46,620
We have now fully derived correspondences

156
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:51,870
between both the unit vectors, i hat j hat and r hat theta hat,

157
00:08:51,870 --> 00:08:58,260
as well as the magnitude r and the relevant magnitudes

158
00:08:58,260 --> 00:09:04,280
x and y for polar and Cartesian coordinate systems.

159
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:05,003


